            <ArticleTitle>Serial quantitative coronary angiography in the assessment of coronary disease in the transplanted heart.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S52-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Quantitative angiographic studies with use of cine-videodensitometry after maximal coronary vasodilation with nitroglycerin in 18 &quot;angiographically normal&quot; heart transplant recipients demonstrated significant loss of lumen diameter between years 1 and 3. When sensitive angiographic techniques are used, graft arteriopathy appears to be ubiquitous in heart transplant recipients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
